    "head_commit_message": "refactor(sim): groups and the split in the crate (spec 39 step 5a)\n\nThe split (split.rs) decides which of a group's units fallen behind split\noff, in what order and where each new group's front is; forming up\n(groups.rs) finds the groups near enough, the gap between their bodies and\nwhat each meeting does, in turn, on the groups as earlier meetings left\nthem. GroupSplit and FormationGroups are views that hand the crate what it\ndoesn't hold and make the new groups, take groups in and send units back.\nGroupPairs and its gdUnit test are gone; their scenarios are cargo tests.\n\nStep 5 splits into 5a (this) and 5b (compaction, reinforce, strays,\nrendezvous, staging), recorded in the spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EVtKBR5V6sRYsnREHZsmii",
